  "preregistration": "Written and committed BEFORE any model extraction on these documents (SC-T12). Expected findings follow from the seeded differences in tools/benchmark/src/fresh-scopecheck.ts. Quotation A (positioned table): LB-3110 quantity 8 -> 6; LB-3115 specification \"1 mg\" for \"0.1 mg\"; FD-4202 specification IP65 for IP68; FD-4215 absent; CL-6401 described with a standard (ISO-17034) next to its own reference, so its identity is uncertain and the requirement stays unmatched; one exclusion. Quotation B (prose): LB-3101 quantity 6 -> 5; LB-3102 specification 0-100 NTU for 0-1000 NTU; SP-5302 absent; two exclusions on separate lines (VAT, carriage). NOT differences, so no finding is expected: quotation A LB-3101 specification is \"c/w 0.01 pH resolution\" (a leading connector); every other row agrees. Absences are Needs review while coverage is unverified; the two with stateIfCoverageConfirmed become confirmed only if coverage is confirmed. CL-6401 stays Needs review either way. Wrapped descriptions (LB-3115 and FD-4215 in the tender, LB-3115 in quotation A): the description continues on a second line, evidence cannot span two lines, so the labelled item value is the first line. Block ids are fixed by the layout (PAGE_ROWS rows per page). Labels are never read by extraction, chunking or matching.",
